ARCHIVE SUMMARY — FIRST SHINOBI WORLD WAR
Konohagakure Historical Records

The First Shinobi World War was the earliest of the great conflicts among
the newly-formed hidden villages, drawing in the Five Great Nations and
numerous smaller lands.

Konoha's Position:
- The village, founded by the First Hokage Hashirama Senju, entered the
  war as an established power. Following Hashirama's death, his brother
  Tobirama Senju led as Second Hokage.
- The Second Hokage fell during this era, sacrificing himself to allow his
  comrades to escape an ambush by Cloud forces, and naming Hiruzen
  Sarutobi as his successor.

Outcome: The war ended without decisive resolution, setting the stage for
recurring conflict. Its principal lesson, recorded by later Hokage, was
the terrible cost of shinobi warfare to each new generation — the very
concern that inspired the village's founding ideals.

Retained for historical instruction. See the founding decree.
